{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1127080-sticking-to-paradigm","id":1127080,"title":"Sticking to paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-10T06:12:13-07:00","id":1127080,"title":"Sticking to paradigm","content":"How close do your games stick to the process of the paradigm of the caster?<br /> <br /> I'm not referring to creating effects outside of the paradigm of the Mage but to how tightly your games stay within the &quot;actual and mythical&quot; framework of the paradigm. <br /> <br /> For instance, we always joked about my SoE character who wore a hat with rods protruding upward holding an aluminium foil tent to shield him from the mind reading powers of aliens for a Mind 1 mental shield effect. If he didn't have the hat then no effect.<br /> <br /> On a deeper note almost every effect my Bata'a Vodoun casts requires a small ritual. There is no quick effects for him and many effects can only be done through first comuning with the spirits which requires a summoning effect as well.<br /> <br /> Now I'm not complaining about either paradigm or the way they work themselves out. I've just noticed that as a player I insist on sticking to the paradigm 100% though when I actually play I'm the only player so this is easier. As a ST (with 4 players) I'm usually very strict on the players telling me exactly how they create each effect. Especially the first time. After the game goes on awhile I notice I start hand waving a lot of effects for time sake. Before long I've noticed that when we get into heated moments in the game my players start to drift from their paradigm and just throw out effects by sphere capabilities. Honestly it probably more my fault than theirs due to the glossing over of effects as the game goes on.<br /> <br /> Do you have these issues as well? How do you keep on track without spending too much time on casting details?<br /> <br /> On a side note we do not use Rotes. Though I'm thinking that having my player write down how they perform their most common effects, paradigm wise, and then do the same for any new elaborate effect might help keep them grounded.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T06:49:20-07:00","id":1127093,"title":"","content":"Every time a player announces they're going to use a sphere effect of some kind I always ask &quot;ok, how do you do that?&quot; Every time. <br /> <br /> I make sure they think about the effect and how their character would accomplish this. I've had a few instances where asking this and making them think through it allowed them the time to come up with a beautiful example of role playing. <br /> <br /> In other circumstances they had thought of an effect they wanted to accomplish but couldn't find a way to justify how their character would do it, and either decided on another action or they asked the others for help figuring out an in character description.<br /> <br /> I feel like Paradigm is never something to slack on. No time spent fleshing it out is wasted time. If it takes longer to tell a story because we're role playing that just makes the experience all the better. But that's just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:24:27-07:00","id":1127098,"title":"","content":"I allow quick effects, but there is always a price for being illprepared. At the lighter end of the scale I'll just impose the fast casting penalty, but I might also introduce little concequences depending on how they do their effect.<br /> <br /> For example, if they drink alcohol as a focus, doing anything more than a couple of ar\u00eate rolls is going to incite a few stamina rolls for inibriation. Drawing lots of shapes and runes on the ground are going to remain there for anyone to see if you don't specifically try to clear them up afterwards. Using fire will lead to burns, and calling spirits will attract other sprits who might be listening in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T07:31:57-07:00","id":1127104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tuch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1127080-sticking-to-paradigm#post1127080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you have these issues as well? How do you keep on track without spending too much time on casting details?<br /> <br /> On a side note we do not use Rotes. Though I'm thinking that having my player write down how they perform their most common effects, paradigm wise, and then do the same for any new elaborate effect might help keep them grounded.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?</div> </div> </div> </div>I enforce paradigm a lot, and in my game the idea of discarding tools/paradigm is removed. So far as the effect fits the theme of the mage is all good.<br /> <br /> Rotes are useful because they are a way for Player to make up effects that they think they will use a lot, write them down for me to greenlight them before hand and we dont lose time on the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}